## MDX Syntax Guidelines and Validation

### Critical MDX Syntax Requirements

MDX files (`.mdx`) require special attention to syntax because they combine Markdown with JSX. Follow these guidelines to prevent parsing errors that break Storybook builds.

#### HTML Entity Escaping (MANDATORY)
```mdx
<!-- ✅ CORRECT - Escape less-than signs -->
- **Load Time**: &lt;20ms component initialization
- **Performance**: &lt;100ms rendering time
- **Target Range**: Values &lt;50% are optimal

<!-- ❌ INCORRECT - Will cause "Unexpected character" errors -->
- **Load Time**: <20ms component initialization
- **Performance**: <100ms rendering time  
- **Target Range**: Values <50% are optimal
```

#### Special Character Handling
```mdx
<!-- ✅ CORRECT - Safe percentage usage -->
- 32% increase in user engagement
- Performance improved by 45%
- **Success Rate**: 28% improvement

<!-- ✅ CORRECT - Escaped angle brackets -->
- **Range**: Values between 10% and &lt;90%
- **Memory**: &lt;500MB typical usage

<!-- ❌ INCORRECT - Problematic bold + percentage combinations -->
- **32% increase** in user engagement (can cause parsing issues)
- **<50% range** for optimal performance (double problem)
```

#### Number-Starting Tags Prevention
```mdx
<!-- ✅ CORRECT - No JSX interpretation -->
Use &lt;20ms for optimal performance

<!-- ❌ INCORRECT - MDX tries to parse as JSX tag -->
Use <20ms for optimal performance
```

### Pre-Development Validation Checklist

Before creating or editing any `.mdx` files:

- [ ] **Scan for `<` followed by numbers**: Replace with `&lt;`
- [ ] **Check percentage signs in bold text**: Simplify formatting if needed
- [ ] **Validate special characters**: Escape `<`, `>`, `&` when not part of intentional HTML
- [ ] **Test locally**: Always run Storybook locally before committing
- [ ] **Check browser console**: Look for MDX parsing errors during development

### Linting and Validation Setup

#### Recommended Linting Configuration
Add to your project's `.eslintrc.js` or similar:

```javascript
// ESLint configuration for MDX files
module.exports = {
  overrides: [
    {
      files: ["**/*.mdx"],
      extends: ["plugin:mdx/recommended"],
      rules: {
        // Prevent common MDX syntax issues
        "mdx/no-unescaped-entities": "error",
        "mdx/no-jsx-in-markdown": "warn"
      }
    }
  ]
};
```

#### Pre-commit Hook (Recommended)
```bash
# Add to .husky/pre-commit or similar
#!/bin/sh
echo "Validating MDX syntax..."

# Check for unescaped less-than signs followed by numbers
if grep -r "<[0-9]" packages/storybook/src/stories/ --include="*.mdx"; then
    echo "❌ Found unescaped < followed by numbers in MDX files"
    echo "Replace with &lt; to fix MDX parsing errors"
    exit 1
fi

# Check for potential problematic percentage patterns
if grep -r "\*\*[0-9][0-9]*%[^*]*\*\*" packages/storybook/src/stories/ --include="*.mdx"; then
    echo "⚠️  Found potentially problematic bold percentage formatting"
    echo "Consider simplifying formatting to avoid MDX parsing issues"
fi

echo "✅ MDX syntax validation passed"
```

#### Manual Validation Commands
```bash
# Quick syntax check for common issues
cd packages/storybook

# Find unescaped less-than signs
grep -r "<[0-9]" src/stories/ --include="*.mdx"

# Find potential percentage formatting issues  
grep -r "\*\*.*%.*\*\*" src/stories/ --include="*.mdx"

# Test Storybook build
npm run build-storybook
```

### Common MDX Pitfalls and Solutions

#### 1. Performance Metrics
```mdx
<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
### Technical Performance
- **Load Time**: &lt;20ms component initialization
- **Memory Usage**: Under 500KB per component
- **Rendering**: &lt;100ms for complex layouts

<!-- ❌ INCORRECT -->
### Technical Performance  
- **Load Time**: <20ms component initialization
- **Memory Usage**: <500KB per component
- **Rendering**: <100ms for complex layouts
```

#### 2. Mathematical Ranges
```mdx
<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
- Optimal range: 10% to &lt;90%
- Performance threshold: &lt;50ms response time
- Error rate: Keep below &lt;1% for production

<!-- ❌ INCORRECT -->
- Optimal range: 10% to <90%
- Performance threshold: <50ms response time  
- Error rate: Keep below <1% for production
```

#### 3. Code Examples in MDX
```mdx
<!-- ✅ CORRECT - Use code blocks for HTML -->
```html
<spectrum-button size="large">
  Click me
</spectrum-button>
\```

<!-- ❌ INCORRECT - Raw HTML in markdown -->
Use <spectrum-button> with size="large" for prominence
```

#### 4. Bold Formatting with Special Characters
```mdx
<!-- ✅ CORRECT - Simple formatting -->
**Business Value:**
- 32% increase in user engagement
- 45% improvement in task completion
- 28% reduction in support tickets

<!-- ❌ PROBLEMATIC - Bold around percentages -->
**Business Value:**
- **32% increase** in user engagement
- **45% improvement** in task completion
- **28% reduction** in support tickets
```

